\textbf{Class:} Non-thrust propulsion architecture \\
\textbf{Principle:} Motion emerges from stability bias \\
\textbf{Core Mechanism:} Forward stability well generation \\
\textbf{Primary Inputs:} Cosmic telemetry, Pt/U plasma states, entropy spikes \\
\textbf{Primary Output:} Stability-gradient drift vector

\section*{2. Field Definitions}
SGPE constructs two primary fields:
\begin{align}
    \Phi_{ext} &= f(\text{NSM}, \text{CRF}, \text{Spectroscopy}) \\
    \Phi_{int} &= g(\text{Pt/U Plasma}, \text{MHD Confinement})
\end{align}
where $\Phi_{ext}$ is the external astrophysical stability field and 
$\Phi_{int}$ is the internal fusion stability anchor.

The stability gradient is defined as:
\begin{equation}
    \nabla \Phi = \Phi_{ext} - \Phi_{int}
\end{equation}

